-// clk_mem (108 MHz). Sampling clk_vid signals on clk_mem caused metastable
-// sync signals that the MiSTer scaler could never lock to → permanent black.
-// The MPEG2 core's outputs are already on clk_mem (dot_clk=clk_mem), so
-// wiring them directly is clean. Before a stream is decoded, the core
-// outputs black (Y=16, Cb=Cr=128), which is fine — "no signal" until play.
+// The decoder's video pipeline runs on dot_clk = clk_sys = CLK_VIDEO (27 MHz),
+// advancing one pixel per ce_pix (13.5 MHz, the BT.601 480i dot rate). All
+// decoder video outputs (RGB, h/v/c_sync, pixel_en, v_pos) are therefore in the
+// CLK_VIDEO domain — no CDC. We register them on ce_pix so they line up with the
+// CE_PIXEL the analog PHY samples, and derive the interlace field flag VGA_F1
+// from the decoder's field parity.
+//
+// Field parity: syncgen encodes the field in v_pos[0] when interlaced
+// (syncgen.v: v_pos = {v_cntr[10:0], ~odd_field}), so v_pos[0] == ~odd_field.
+// MiSTer convention: VGA_F1 = 1 on the second (odd) field. odd_field == ~v_pos[0],
+// so VGA_F1 = ~core_v_pos[0]. Latched on ce_pix in the CLK_VIDEO domain so it is
+// stable for the whole field the PHY/DAC is emitting.
+//
